=== Module 11 - NFA and epsilon-NFA ===

--- fixtures/ends-abb.nfa   (nondeterministic, for (a|b)*abb) ---
states: S S1 S2 S3    alphabet: a b
start: S    accept: S3
  S has TWO transitions on 'a':  S -a-> S   and   S -a-> S1   (the 'guess')

run "aabb"  (tracking the SET of possible states):
  after start  {S}
  after a      {S,S1}
  after a      {S,S1}
  after b      {S,S2}
  after b      {S,S3}
  final set contains S3 (accepting)?  true   -> ACCEPT

cross-check, all up to length 6:
  NFA language == DFA language (Module 10):  true   (15 strings)
  every NFA-accepted string is regex-matched:  true

--- fixtures/ab-star.nfa   (epsilon-NFA for (a|b)*) ---
has epsilon transitions?  true

epsilon-closure of {I} (the start):  {A1,B1,F,I,U}
  -> before reading any input, the NFA is 'in' all of these at once,
     including F, so the empty string is accepted (zero repetitions).

run "ab":
  after start  {A1,B1,F,I,U}
  after a      {A1,A2,B1,F,U,W}
  after b      {A1,B1,B2,F,U,W}

removeEpsilon():  new NFA has epsilon transitions?  false
  new accepting states: I A2 B2 W F   (every state whose epsilon-closure reached the old F)
  L(epsilon-NFA) == L(epsilon-free NFA), up to length 5:  true
  ...and both == regex (a|b)*:  true
  language: epsilon, a, b, aa, ab, ba, bb, aaa, aab, aba, ...

summary: NFA(a|b)*abb == DFA == regex (true) | epsilon-closure computed | epsilon removed, language unchanged (true) -> epsilon and nondeterminism add NO power
